ated uses the global ngroups for group_size under tensor parallelism", "source_excerpt": "[Bug] Mamba2 RMSNormGated uses the global ngroups for group_size under tensor parallelism\n### Summary\n\nWith tensor parallelism, `Mamba2` builds its gated RMSNorm with a group size that is `world_size` times too small ([mamba2.py#L144-L145](https://github.com/state-spaces/mamba/blob/e9594ce1c732d97440f0332fdc43170a2294dbfa/mamba_ssm/modules/mamba2.py#L144-L145)):\n\n```python\nself.norm = RMSNormGated", "third_party_claim": "关键词检索候选，需人工确认是否讨论论文结果。", "third_party": null, "author_response": null, "resolution_status": "open", "resolution_url": null, "observed_at": "2026-10-09T04:41:11.575316Z", "confidence": null, "limitations": ["未运行代码；关键词命中不能证明复现成功或失败。", "作者身份仅依据显式提供的 author_logins。"], "comments": []}, "internal_evidence": [], "external_source_urls": ["https://github.com/state-spaces/mamba/issues/1047"], "checked_at": "2026-10-09T04:41:11.575316Z", "uncertainty": "第三方公开线索；系统没有运行代码。关闭 issue 不等于结果已复现。"}, {"finding_id": "f-signal-repo-597ab80a4c0e-1024", "dimension_id": "code_reproduction_signals", "severity": "info", "status": "pending_verification", "title": "discussion_inconclusive", "description": "关键词检索候选，需人工确认是否讨论论文结果。", "reproduction_signal": {"signal_id": "signal-repo-597ab80a4c0e-1024", "repository_id": "repo-597ab80a4c0e", "signal_type": "discussion_inconclusive", "review_status": "candidate", "source_url": "https://github.com/state-spaces/mamba/issues/1024", "source_title": "Mamba3 step() is non-deterministic and does not match forward()", "source_excerpt": "Mamba3 step() is non-deterministic and does not match forward()\n## Question\n\nI have noticed there is an output difference between calling `step()` and `forward()`.\n\nWhen using the same model and feeding in the exact same input sequence, invoking `Mamba3.forward()` directly versus running multiple `Mamba3.step()` calls in a loop yields outputs that diverge noticeably, with a maximum difference valu", "third_party_claim": "关键词检索候选，需人工确认是否讨论论文结果。", "third_party": null, "author_response": null, "resolution_status": "open", "resolution_url": null, "observed_at": "2026-10-09T04:41:11.577335Z", "confidence": null, "limitations": ["未运行代码；关键词命中不能证明复现成功或失败。", "作者身份仅依据显式提供的 author_logins。"], "comments": [{"source_url": "https://github.com/state-spaces/mamba/issues/1024#issuecomment-5717569384", "excerpt": "Root cause identified: OOB writes when headdim < tile_D (hardcoded 64)\nThe reporter''s config uses headdim=16, but step() hardcodes tile_D=64 (mamba3.py L402/L425). The kernel launches grid = ceil_div(mState.shape[2]=16, 64) = 1 (mamba3_step_fn.py L221) while each block reads or writes a 64-wide tile of state and output with no bounds checking (# Load State, not doing any bound check for now, L384)", "login": "imao81"}, {"source_url": "https://github.com/state-spaces/mamba/issues/1024#issuecomment-5727940101", "excerpt": "Fix submitted in #1046: shape-based routing — SISO configs with headdim % 64 != 0 fall back to the existing Triton step kernel (bitwise-deterministic, no param corruption, step-vs-forward ~6.5e-3); CuTe path bit-exact unchanged; unsafe configs raise NotImplementedError.", "login": "imao81"}]}, "internal_evidence": [], "external_source_urls": ["https://github.com/state-spaces/mamba/issues/1024"], "checked_at": "2026-10-09T04:41:11.577335Z", "uncertainty": "第三方公开线索；系统没有运行代码。关闭 issue 不等于结果已复现。"}, {"finding_id": "f-signal-repo-597ab80a4c0e-1022", "dimension_id": "code_reproduction_signals", "severity": "info", "status": "pending_verification", "title": "discussion_inconclusive", "description": "关键词检索候选，需人工确认是否讨论论文结果。", "reproduction_signal": {"signal_id": "signal-repo-597ab80a4c0e-1022", "repository_id": "repo-597ab80a4c0e", "signal_type": "discussion_inconclusive", "review_status": "candidate", "source_url": "https://github.com/state-spaces/mamba/issues/1022#issuecomment-5431600555", "source_title": "Mamba-3 incremental decode broken: `step()` receives `(B, 1, D)` but `_preprocess` expects 2-D — EinopsError in `.generate()` for both official 1.5B checkpoints", "source_excerpt": "One addition from the tilelang side (tile-ai/tilelang#3071): the tilelang maintainers recommend using `T.dynamic` for the Mamba-3 MIMO kernel spec so a single compiled kernel serves arbitrary seqlens. Currently every distinct seqlen triggers a full ~7-8s JIT recompile (one cache key per shape), which makes token-by-token generation impractical on the MIMO path (~8s/token) independent of the `step(", "third_party_claim": "关键词检索候选，需人工确认是否讨论论文结果。", "third_party": null, "author_response": null, "resolution_status": "open", "resolution_url": null, "observed_at": "2026-10-09T04:41:11.579128Z", "confidence": null, "limitations": ["未运行代码；关键词命中不能证明复现成功或失败。", "作者身份仅依据显式提供的 author_logins。"], "comments": [{"source_url": "https://github.com/state-spaces/mamba/issues/1022#issuecomment-5384259745", "excerpt": "The tilelang-side companion issue (silent all-zeros MIMO kernel miscompilation on sm_121, compile-order-dependent) is now filed: https://github.com/tile-ai/tilelang/issues/3071", "login": "robertforbes68"}, {"source_url": "https://github.com/state-spaces/mamba/issues/1022#issuecomment-5431600555", "excerpt": "One addition from the tilelang side (tile-ai/tilelang#3071): the tilelang maintainers recommend using `T.dynamic` for the Mamba-3 MIMO kernel spec so a single compiled kernel serves arbitrary seqlens. Currently every distinct seqlen triggers a full ~7-8s JIT recompile (one cache key per shape), which makes token-by-token generation impractical on the MIMO path (~8s/token) independent of the `step(", "login": "robertforbes68"}, {"source_url": "https://github.com/state-spaces/mamba/issues/1022#issuecomment-5432020209", "excerpt": "Checkpoint observation while investigating what we initially misdiagnosed as a kernel bug (tile-ai/tilelang#3071, now resolved as not-tilelang): `mamba3-mimo-1.5b` has a content-triggered degenerate attractor. Greedy generation from \"Inventory record: the component serial number is CN-4821 … The serial number of that component is\" produces an endless \"000000…\" loop — reproducible across prompt var", "login": "robertforbes68"}, {"source_url": "https://github.com/state-spaces/mamba/issues/1022#issuecomment-5518700159", "excerpt": "Data point on the `T.dynamic` question, now that tilelang 0.1.14 is out (Sept 2). Same measurements posted to tile-ai/tilelang#3071.\n\n**Setup:** DGX Spark (GB10, sm_121, driver 580.173.02, torch 2.11 cu130), `mamba3-mimo-1.5b`, mamba-ssm git main (`e9594ce`), isolated `TILELANG_CACHE_DIR` so every new seqlen is a cold compile. Same script, same day; the only variables are the tilelang version and ", "login": "robertforbes68"}]}, "internal_evidence": [], "external_source_urls": ["https://github.com/state-spaces/mamba/issues/1022#issuecomment-5431600555"], "checked_at": "2026-10-09T04:41:11.579128Z", "uncertainty": "第三方公开线索；系统没有运行代码。关闭 issue 不等于结果已复现。"}, {"finding_id": "f-signal-repo-597ab80a4c0e-1019", "dimension_id": "code_reproduction_signals", "severity": "info", "status": "pending_verification", "title": "discussion_inconclusive", "description": "关键词检索候选，需人工确认是否讨论论文结果。", "reproduction_signal": {"signal_id": "signal-repo-597ab80a4c0e-1019", "repository_id": "repo-597ab80a4c0e", "signal_type": "discussion_inconclusive", "review_status": "candidate", "source_url": "https://github.com/state-spaces/mamba/issues/1019", "source_title": "No prebuilt wheels for sm_103 (B300) and sm_121 (GB10)", "source_excerpt": "No prebuilt wheels for sm_103 (B300) and sm_121 (GB10)\n## Problem\n\n`mamba-ssm` does not ship prebuilt wheels for new NVIDIA GPU architectures:\n- **sm_103** (B300 SXM6, GB300)\n- **sm_121** (GB10, DGX Spark / Project DIGITS)\n\nUsers must compile from source, which requires:\n1. Matching CUDA toolkit version (13.0+ for sm_121, 12.8+ for sm_103)\n2. Setting `TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST` correctly\n3. Working aro", "third_party_claim": "关键词检索候选，需人工确认是否讨论论文结果。", "