 i''d  appreciate it\r\n<img width=\"475\" alt=\"截屏2024-01-16 14 20 30\" src=\"https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/assets/112547090/0358ffe7-e5e3-4d37-9f1e-3a61f16b068f\">\r\n", "third_party_claim": "关键词检索候选，需人工确认是否讨论论文结果。", "third_party": null, "author_response": null, "resolution_status": "open", "resolution_url": null, "observed_at": "2026-10-09T04:41:25.623710Z", "confidence": null, "limitations": ["未运行代码；关键词命中不能证明复现成功或失败。", "作者身份仅依据显式提供的 author_logins。"], "comments": [{"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/99#issuecomment-1893275000", "excerpt": "Hi @BBetteroff , DSIR stands for \"Data Selection with Importance Resampling\" (see paper [here](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2302.03169.pdf)) and is used to compute importance weights for each sample with respect to different target domains.\r\n\r\nThe screenshot you posted is from the `prep_artifacts.py` scripts. The flag `--dsir_num_samples` corresponds to the number of samples you use from the target domai", "login": "mauriceweber"}, {"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/99#issuecomment-1893300405", "excerpt": "> Hi @BBetteroff , DSIR stands for \"Data Selection with Importance Resampling\" (see paper [here](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2302.03169.pdf)) and is used to compute importance weights for each sample with respect to different target domains.\r\n> \r\n> The screenshot you posted is from the `prep_artifacts.py` scripts. The flag `--dsir_num_samples` corresponds to the number of samples you use from the target", "login": "BBetteroff"}, {"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/99#issuecomment-1899929591", "excerpt": "what‘s the content of listing file?,can you show me a example? and what''s the use?", "login": "BBetteroff"}, {"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/99#issuecomment-1903430732", "excerpt": "The listing files contain the ids of inputs which, when concatenated with the base uri point to the location of the data. For example:\r\n```\r\n2023-06/0000/de_head.json.gz\r\n2023-06/0000/de_middle.json.gz\r\n2023-06/0000/de_tail.json.gz\r\n2023-06/0000/en_head.json.gz\r\n2023-06/0000/en_middle.json.gz\r\n2023-06/0000/en_tail.json.gz\r\n2023-06/0000/es_head.json.gz\r\n```\r\nFor example, if your data is stored loca", "login": "mauriceweber"}]}, "internal_evidence": [], "external_source_urls": ["https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/99"], "checked_at": "2026-10-09T04:41:25.623710Z", "uncertainty": "第三方公开线索；系统没有运行代码。关闭 issue 不等于结果已复现。"}, {"finding_id": "f-signal-repo-d4c01d613411-97", "dimension_id": "code_reproduction_signals", "severity": "info", "status": "pending_verification", "title": "discussion_inconclusive", "description": "关键词检索候选，需人工确认是否讨论论文结果。", "reproduction_signal": {"signal_id": "signal-repo-d4c01d613411-97", "repository_id": "repo-d4c01d613411", "signal_type": "discussion_inconclusive", "review_status": "candidate", "source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/97", "source_title": "possibly missing shard from host", "source_excerpt": "possibly missing shard from host\nI cannot get a valid shard from\r\nhttps://data.together.xyz/redpajama-data-v2/v1.0.0/documents/2014-52/1940/es_middle.json.gz\r\n\r\ncan anyone else replicate this, or is the issue on my end?", "third_party_claim": "关键词检索候选，需人工确认是否讨论论文结果。", "third_party": null, "author_response": null, "resolution_status": "closed", "resolution_url": null, "observed_at": "2026-10-09T04:41:25.624281Z", "confidence": null, "limitations": ["未运行代码；关键词命中不能证明复现成功或失败。", "作者身份仅依据显式提供的 author_logins。"], "comments": [{"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/97#issuecomment-1885236556", "excerpt": "Hi @sagnak , thanks for flagging that -- there are indeed a few files in the dataset which are broken (a few hundred in total, mostly resulting from failed S3 queries). You can safely skip these.\r\n\r\nSee also the discussion on Huggingface: https://huggingface.co/datasets/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data-V2/discussions/20\r\n\r\n \r\n", "login": "mauriceweber"}, {"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/97#issuecomment-1888160772", "excerpt": "Thanks for the huggingface pointer! Indeed all those aforementioned shards are also broken for me", "login": "sagnak"}]}, "internal_evidence": [], "external_source_urls": ["https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/97"], "checked_at": "2026-10-09T04:41:25.624281Z", "uncertainty": "第三方公开线索；系统没有运行代码。关闭 issue 不等于结果已复现。"}, {"finding_id": "f-signal-repo-d4c01d613411-80", "dimension_id": "code_reproduction_signals", "severity": "info", "status": "pending_verification", "title": "discussion_inconclusive", "description": "关键词检索候选，需人工确认是否讨论论文结果。", "reproduction_signal": {"signal_id": "signal-repo-d4c01d613411-80", "repository_id": "repo-d4c01d613411", "signal_type": "discussion_inconclusive", "review_status": "candidate", "source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/80#issuecomment-1791279518", "source_title": "Executing V2 issues", "source_excerpt": "There is no data that needs to be pulled from an external S3 bucket, only your own where you have the ccnet output stored -- it is also only required to create the artifacts. Are you creating your own artifacts for a custom dataset or are you trying to reproduce the quality signals we have provided?\r\n\r\nYou can download the ccnet out from the public urls (https://data.together.xyz/redpajama-data-v2", "third_party_claim": "关键词检索候选，需人工确认是否讨论论文结果。", "third_party": null, "author_response": null, "resolution_status": "open", "resolution_url": null, "observed_at": "2026-10-09T04:41:25.631106Z", "confidence": null, "limitations": ["未运行代码；关键词命中不能证明复现成功或失败。", "作者身份仅依据显式提供的 author_logins。"], "comments": [{"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/80#issuecomment-1789545586", "excerpt": "I can verify that len(inputs_by_snapsh) is 0\r\n\r\nedit: I seem to not have the listings correct, or the s3 bucket info correct. is it possible to get an example of a listsings.txt and \r\n\r\n\r\nS3_ENDPOINT_URL=\"https://red-pajama.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com\"\r\nS3_BUCKET=\"red-pajama\"\r\nS3_CCNET_PREFIX=\"/rs_cc_net\"\r\nS3_PROFILE=\"default\"\r\n\r\nDOCKER_S3_ENDPOINT_URL=\"https://red-pajama.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com", "login": "hicotton02"}, {"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/80#issuecomment-1790790904", "excerpt": "Hi @hicotton02 , thanks for your question!\r\n\r\n> default.conf is missing lines for the AWS Secret and ID\r\nWe deliberately left these out since so that users specify these via `export AWS_SECRET...` (reduces the risk of uploading access keys to github).\r\n\r\nOnce the environment variables are specified, you can get the listings via\r\n\r\n```bash\r\ns5cmd --profile \"$S3_PROFILE\" --endpoint-url \"$S3_ENDPOINT", "login": "mauriceweber"}, {"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/80#issuecomment-1790971924", "excerpt": "Thank you so much for the response. \r\n\r\nIs the s5cmd command supposed to point to my own s3 bucket or someone else''s?\r\n\r\nI created a bucket but it is blank at this time. I remember in V1 we were downloading info from I think Arxiv''s bucket.\r\n\r\nedit: As part of this workstream, do we download ccnet data separately (I see their repo went archive)?", "login": "hicotton02"}, {"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/80#issuecomment-1791279518", "excerpt": "There is no data that needs to be pulled from an external S3 bucket, only your own where you have the ccnet output stored -- it is also only required to create the artifacts. Are you creating your own artifacts for a custom dataset or are you trying to reproduce the quality signals we have provided?\r\n\r\nYou can download the ccnet out from the public urls (https://data.together.xyz/redpajama-data-v2", "login": "mauriceweber"}, {"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/80#issuecomment-1791329250", "excerpt": "> There is no data that needs to be pulled from an external S3 bucket, only your own where you have the ccnet output stored -- it is also only required to create the artifacts. Are you creating your own artifacts for a custom dataset or are you trying to reproduce the quality signals we have provided?\r\n> \r\n> You can download the ccnet out from the public urls (https://data.together.xyz/redpajama-d", "login": "hicotton02"}, {"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/80#issuecomment-1791849769", "excerpt": "Wrote a python script to download all the ccnet data based on your links above. it does this in parallel and is basic. saturated my connection and server to get the most efficient process going.\r\n\r\n```\r\nimport os\r\nimport subprocess\r\nimport multiprocessing as mp\r\n\r\nCC_SNAPSHOT_IDS = [\r\n  \"2014-15\",\r\n  \"2014-23\",\r\n  \"2014-35\",\r\n  \"2014-41\",\r\n  \"2014-42\",\r\n  \"2014-49\",\r\n  \"2014-52\",\r\n  \"2015-14\",\r\n  ", "login": "hicotton02"}]}, "internal_evidence": [], "external_source_urls": ["https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/80#issuecomment-1791279518"], "checked_at": "2026-10-09T04:41:25.631106Z", "uncertainty": "第三方公开线索；系统没有运行代码。关闭 issue 不等于结果已复现。"}, {"finding_id": "f-signal-repo-d4c01d613411-67", "dimension_id": "code_reproduction_signals", "severity": "info", "status": "pending_verification", "title": "discussion_inconclusive", "description": "关键词检索候选，需人工确认是否讨论论文结果。", "reproduction_signal": {"signal_id": "signal-repo-d4c01d613411-67", "repository_id": "repo-d4c01d613411", "signal_type": "discussion_inconclusive", "review_status": "candidate", "source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/67#issuecomment-1662089029", "source_title": "Failed building wheel for cc-net", "