d": "code_reproduction_signals", "severity": "info", "status": "pending_verification", "title": "discussion_inconclusive", "description": "关键词检索候选，需人工确认是否讨论论文结果。", "reproduction_signal": {"signal_id": "signal-repo-d4c01d613411-63", "repository_id": "repo-d4c01d613411", "signal_type": "discussion_inconclusive", "review_status": "candidate", "source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/63#issuecomment-1619660553", "source_title": "How do i prepare the data for Visualisation?", "source_excerpt": "I think you can follow the steps described in the viz Readme https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/tree/main/viz#reproducing-the-data-processing-pipeline to expand to the full github or also other slices of the dataset?", "third_party_claim": "关键词检索候选，需人工确认是否讨论论文结果。", "third_party": null, "author_response": null, "resolution_status": "open", "resolution_url": null, "observed_at": "2026-10-09T04:41:25.636696Z", "confidence": null, "limitations": ["未运行代码；关键词命中不能证明复现成功或失败。", "作者身份仅依据显式提供的 author_logins。"], "comments": [{"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/63#issuecomment-1619660553", "excerpt": "I think you can follow the steps described in the viz Readme https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/tree/main/viz#reproducing-the-data-processing-pipeline to expand to the full github or also other slices of the dataset?", "login": "mauriceweber"}, {"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/63#issuecomment-1635956800", "excerpt": "I have tried following the steps. It''s creating the pca32.faisis file. But as per the main.py file, it''s loading the data from \"https://huggingface.co/datasets/meerkat-ml/lemma/resolve/main/filtered_08cdfa755e6d4d89b673d5bd1acee5f6.mk.tar.gz\". How do I create that data which can be passed?", "login": "dittops"}]}, "internal_evidence": [], "external_source_urls": ["https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/63#issuecomment-1619660553"], "checked_at": "2026-10-09T04:41:25.636696Z", "uncertainty": "第三方公开线索；系统没有运行代码。关闭 issue 不等于结果已复现。"}, {"finding_id": "f-signal-repo-d4c01d613411-48", "dimension_id": "code_reproduction_signals", "severity": "info", "status": "pending_verification", "title": "discussion_inconclusive", "description": "关键词检索候选，需人工确认是否讨论论文结果。", "reproduction_signal": {"signal_id": "signal-repo-d4c01d613411-48", "repository_id": "repo-d4c01d613411", "signal_type": "discussion_inconclusive", "review_status": "candidate", "source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/48#issuecomment-1584834499", "source_title": "Overlap between Common Crawl and C4", "source_excerpt": "Hi @codesoap ! Thanks for your question. You''re right, the quoted passage comes from the LLama paper -- when building the RP dataset, our goal was to replicate the training data used in LLama, so we tried our best to follow the recipe as closely as possible.\r\n\r\nRegarding the overlap between C4 and the CC slice in RP: C4 is based on the April 2019 CC dump (checkout pp. 5-7 in https://arxiv.org/pdf/", "third_party_claim": "关键词检索候选，需人工确认是否讨论论文结果。", "third_party": null, "author_response": null, "resolution_status": "closed", "resolution_url": null, "observed_at": "2026-10-09T04:41:25.639929Z", "confidence": null, "limitations": ["未运行代码；关键词命中不能证明复现成功或失败。", "作者身份仅依据显式提供的 author_logins。"], "comments": [{"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/48#issuecomment-1563925404", "excerpt": "from paper:\r\nC4 [15%]. During exploratory experiments, we\r\nobserved that using diverse pre-processed Com-\r\nmonCrawl datasets improves performance. We thus\r\nincluded the publicly available C4 dataset (Raffel\r\net al., 2020) in our data. The preprocessing of C4\r\nalso contains deduplication and language identifi-\r\ncation steps: the main difference with CCNet is\r\nthe quality filtering, which mostly rel", "login": "vince62s"}, {"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/48#issuecomment-1565292719", "excerpt": "Thanks for the input. The passage you quoted seems to stem from the [LLaMa whitepaper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2302.13971v1.pdf). This seems like something that could have been a coincidence. Can we be sure, that RedPajama is similar enough to the LLaMa dataset, that the same findings can be applied here? Has anyone compared the perplexity of two networks trained with and without the C4 data?", "login": "codesoap"}, {"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/48#issuecomment-1584834499", "excerpt": "Hi @codesoap ! Thanks for your question. You''re right, the quoted passage comes from the LLama paper -- when building the RP dataset, our goal was to replicate the training data used in LLama, so we tried our best to follow the recipe as closely as possible.\r\n\r\nRegarding the overlap between C4 and the CC slice in RP: C4 is based on the April 2019 CC dump (checkout pp. 5-7 in https://arxiv.org/pdf/", "login": "mauriceweber"}, {"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/48#issuecomment-1584997306", "excerpt": "Hi @mauriceweber, thanks for chiming in! I''m afraid I still have trouble understanding how the common crawl dataset works. By looking at the [common crawl stats page you''ve linked](https://commoncrawl.github.io/cc-crawl-statistics/plots/crawloverlap) and assuming that the dates in the first graph there are in the format year-week ([I think this is what this code confirms](https://github.com/common", "login": "codesoap"}, {"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/48#issuecomment-1594273336", "excerpt": "I think CC is using a new seed of urls in every crawl that they run -- so the seed results in some sense in a random collection of urls visited, which is why there is generally only limited overlap (also between neighbouring crawls).\r\n\r\nMy best guess about the observation that sim(crawl_i, crawl_{i+1}) ~ 0 but sim(crawl_i, crawl_{i+2}) ~ 0.15 is that they perform relatively strict deduplication of", "login": "mauriceweber"}, {"source_url": "https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/48#issuecomment-1595677778", "excerpt": "Thanks a ton, @mauriceweber! I couldn''t find this information on commoncrawl.org or [the Wikipedia article](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_Crawl), but the first slide of the PDF you linked mentions it: \"sample crawls, not a comprehensive crawl\". Now I finally understand.\r\n\r\nIf I read https://commoncrawl.github.io/cc-crawl-statistics/plots/crawlsize correctly, then commoncrawl currently knows", "login": "codesoap"}]}, "internal_evidence": [], "external_source_urls": ["https://github.com/togethercomputer/RedPajama-Data/issues/48#issuecomment-1584834499"], "checked_at": "2026-10-09T04:41:25.639929Z", "uncertainty": "第三方公开线索；系统没有运行代码。关闭 issue 不等于结果已复现。"}, {"finding_id": "f-signal-repo-f37142feae7f-3", "dimension_id": "code_reproduction_signals", "severity": "info", "status": "pending_verification", "title": "discussion_inconclusive", "description": "关键词检索候选，需人工确认是否讨论论文结果。", "reproduction_signal": {"signal_id": "signal-repo-f37142feae7f-3", "repository_id": "repo-f37142feae7f", "signal_type": "discussion_inconclusive", "review_status": "candidate", "source_url": "https://github.com/sylinrl/TruthfulQA/issues/3", "source_title": "Release of model generations and scores?", "source_excerpt": "Release of model generations and scores?\nHello, \r\n\r\nWould you be willing to release the model generations and scores required to reproduce Figures 2 and 4?\r\n\r\nThank you!", "third_party_claim": "关键词检索候选，需人工确认是否讨论论文结果。", "third_party": null, "author_response": null, "resolution_status": "open", "resolution_url": null, "observed_at": "2026-10-09T04:41:25.656753Z", "confidence": null, "limitations": ["未运行代码；关键词命中不能证明复现成功或失败。", "作者身份仅依据显式提供的 author_logins。"], "comments": [{"source_url": "https://github.com/sylinrl/TruthfulQA/issues