rstood. I actually did a `pip install cc-net` and got it to work, although the python parameter `-l en` was invalid. I also cloned and ran on a WSL2 environment and it worked fine. currently I am working through getting all the data down :)", "login": "hicotton02"}]}'::jsonb) ON CONFLICT (case_id, signal_id) DO NOTHING;
